Section 9.5 evidence records. Six transactions carry a 32-byte content at offsets
0, 4, 32, 36, at 5 (off alignment), and truncated to 20 bytes. The evidence record
carries the calldata and nothing else: the scanner never decides provenness. The
offline core proves the first four and leaves the last two unproven, since section
9.5 reads the content only at a multiple of 32 or 4 plus a multiple of 32, wholly
within the calldata.
